  "fields": {
    "title": "Media Queries",
    "textContent": {
      "nodeType": "document",
      "data": {},
      "content": [
        {
          "nodeType": "heading-3",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Description",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Media queries let you apply CSS styles depending on a device's screen resolution or browser viewport width or other characteristics. Media queries are used for targeting media features (like ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "hover, color, device width, display mode ",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "or ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "orientation",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": ") or media types (",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "all, print",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": " or ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "screen",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "). That's for example useful for making websites ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "2ABYnMzPbdcoVRHCQpEav8",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "responsive",
                  "marks": [],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": ". ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "There are different ways to use media queries for making a site responsive: you can for example initially style your page for mobile devices and then use media queries to set the styling for larger screens. This approach is called ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "4IfiJSNdpxkRvG3b4pTIuP",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "mobile first",
                  "marks": [],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": ". But you can of course also start with desktop screens and then later adjust the layout for smaller displays. You can also use media queries, for example, to check whether users have activated light or dark mode and adjust the colours of your page depending on this.",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "While coding a website, you can check the appearance of your site on different screen sizes by resizing your browser window or with the help of the ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "3kpgl4hPVcbTfdNGnwPfUJ",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "developer tools",
                  "marks": [],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": " in your browser. You can switch between different screen sizes by toggling the device toolbar on the top left corner of the dev tools.",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "codeField": {
      "data": {},
      "content": [
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "code"
                }
              ],
              "value": "css\n/* Desktop Size and Light Mode*/\nbody{\n  font-size: 16px;\n  background-color: white;\n  color: black;\n}\n/* Tablet Size */\n@media (max-width: 900px) {\n  body{\n      font-size: 14px;\n  }\n}\n/* Mobile Size */\n@media (max-width: 400px) {\n  body{\n      font-size: 12px;\n  }\n}\n/* when dark mode is active */ \n@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {\n  body{\n    background-color: black;\n    color: white;\n  }\n}",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        }
      ],
      "nodeType": "document"
    },
